            // production (Somerville et al. 2014, FAO Fisheries and Aquaculture Technical Paper
            // 589, https://www.fao.org/4/i4021e/i4021e.pdf, read 2026-09-27), section 7.3: "The
            // suggested rate is 5–8 litres of air per minute for each cubic metre of water,
            // coming from at least 2 air stones in different locations in the fish tank", so this
            // 1.6 x 1.0 x 1.6 m tank, 2.56 m3, wants 12.8 to 20.5 L a minute at the bottom of about
            // a metre of water. The pump: a HIBLOW HP-20 linear air pump, whose spec sheet
            // (https://www.hiblow-usa.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/HP-20-40_170119.pdf, read
            // 2026-09-27) gives "Rated Loading Pressure kPa 9.8" (a metre of water), "Airflow
            // Volume" 20 L/min at 60 Hz and "Power Consumption W 17": the top of FAO's range, for
            // 17 W. FAO wants the aeration on around the clock ("simple battery backups for air
            // pumps have saved countless fish"), so it is a steady load, priority 1, shed last.
            power: Some(Consumer(
                watts: 17.0,
                priority: 1,
