            // Energy (2026-09-27; it charged its 500 W for 24 hours, 12.0 kWh a day). EIA, 2020
            // Residential Energy Consumption Survey, Table CE5.3a "Detailed household site
            // electricity end-use consumption, part 1 - averages" (released June 2023, revised
            // March 2024, https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/c&e/xls/ce5.3a.xlsx,
            // read 2026-09-27): clothes washers, "3 members", 77 kWh a year per household using
            // one, 8.8 W averaged over the year. That is the machine's own draw: RECS defines a
            // clothes washer as "powered by an electric motor" and counts the water it heats under
            // water heating, "The use of energy to heat water for domestic hot water"
            // (https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/terminology.php, read 2026-09-27), which
            // the water heater below carries. How often: RECS 2020 Table HC3.4 (final release March
            // 2023, https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/hc/xls/HC%203.4.xlsx, read
            // 2026-09-27) finds 9.56 million three-person homes washing "1 to 4 loads per week",
            // 5.25 million "5 to 9" and 1.30 million 10 or more; at the bins' midpoints (a game
            // estimate) that is about 4.8 loads a week, so about 0.3 kWh a load for the motor.
            // `watts` is what the electrical sim draws around the clock (it has no model of a
            // wash cycle), so it carries the same 8.8 W average; the port keeps the 500 W motor,
            // which sizes the cable. The home_solo.ron washer is the same machine for one person.
            // Its water (2026-09-27; it had only a cold feed): a machine sold in North America
            // takes a hot and a cold hose and mixes them for a warm wash, and the measured homes
            // above draw "Clothes washers ... 20.0" percent of its water hot. 33 L a day (11 a
            // person), 6.6 of it hot from the water heater.
            power: Some(Consumer(
                watts: 8.8,
