            label: "Solar panel",
            category: "Power",
            stats: [
                (
                    kind: "power",
                    value: "+1.1 kWh/d a year's average here, 0.5 in January",
                    status: "ok",
                ),
            ],
            // What a panel makes at the home's site (2026-09-27; the meter counted 400 W x 4.5
            // sun-hours with no losses, 1.8 kWh a day, and the Energy loop 1.44 at a generic 4.5
            // sun-hours x 0.80). The site is data/self_sufficiency/location.ron's Silverdale, WA.
            // NREL's PVWatts calculator (version 8.5.0, now served by the National Laboratory of
            // the Rockies, https://developer.nlr.gov/api/pvwatts/v8.json, queried 2026-09-27) for
            // lat 47.645, lon -122.695, one 0.4 kW panel, fixed open rack, tilt 40 degrees facing
            // south (a game choice, near the latitude, which favours winter), PVWatts' default
            // 14.08% system losses, weather "NSRDB PSM V3 GOES tmy-2020": "ac_annual" 440.6776
            // kWh a year at the inverter, "solrad_annual" 3.9062 kWh/m2/day on the panel,
            // "capacity_factor" 12.576 (per cent); the worst month is January, whose "ac_monthly"
            // is 17.600 kWh (0.568 a day; December 18.983). An
            // off-grid home time-shifts most of it through its batteries: Tesla's Powerwall 2
            // datasheet gives "Round Trip Efficiency 90%" ("AC to battery to AC, at beginning of
            // life", read 2026-09-27), taken on all of it as data/home_outline.json does (the share
            // used while the sun is up skips the battery, so this is the cautious end). So
            // 440.68 kWh x 0.90 / 8,760 h = 45.3 W averaged, 1.09 kWh a day, 0.51 in January. The
            // live sim still follows the game's own sun with the 400 W peak.
            power: Some(Solar(
                peak_watts: 400.0,
                average_watts: Some(45.3),
            )),
            ports: [],
            storage: [],
            auto_recipe: None,
            container_type: None,
            model: None,
        ),
