        // In-world screens (rung 3): a camera post. A thin 1.7 m post
        // whose head (the top of the post) carries the lens; a screen with
        // screen_source "camera:<this instance's id>" shows what it sees.
        // `camera` is (yaw, pitch, fov) in degrees: yaw 0 = the post's
        // front (-Z at rotation 0) and the placed instance's rotation adds
        // to it; pitch -8 looks a little down like a mounted camera; a 70
        // degree lens. `camera_px` is the size the camera RENDERS at, not
        // the wall's px: the cost of a camera view is per pixel (measured
        // 2026-09-18: a 1280 x 720 re-render was 17 ms, a full extra scene
        // pass in a 10 fps room), so 640 x 360 is a quarter of the wall's
        // pixels for about a quarter of the cost; the wall stretches it.
        "camera_post": (
            shape: "box",
            size: (0.14, 1.7, 0.14),
            color: (0.2, 0.2, 0.22),
