            supply: "composter (food + crop + human waste) -> fertilizer; returns about N 53% / P 75% / K 93% of uptake (data/home_outline.json audit)",
            closes: false,
            weakest: false,
            note: "Does not close yet (the 2026-09-26 garden model, docs/design/gameplay-gaps-2026-09-25.md). Three residents\' urine would cover the garden\'s nitrogen with a little to spare if the body and the garden ran on one clock, but phosphorus and potassium would still need compost and outside inputs. In play the body runs on real time while the garden runs about 720 times faster, so one player\'s urine is a fraction of a percent of what the garden takes. Compost releases its nitrogen slowly over years, and legumes fix some of their own.",
